spirv-tools: accept CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Generic (treat as Linux, timers off)

STK bundles shaderc, whose third_party/spirv-tools CMakeLists dispatches on
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME and FATAL_ERRORs on anything unknown ("Your platform
'Generic' is not supported!"). A bare Phoenix cross build uses Generic, so
configure aborts here even though the GLES2/SP renderer never invokes the
Vulkan/SPIR-V path at runtime.

Add a Generic branch mirroring the Linux one — the same way STK already added a
NintendoSwitch branch just below. SPIRV_LINUX only selects ANSI colour codes in
source/print.cpp. Unlike the Linux branch we do NOT enable SPIRV_TIMER_ENABLED:
Phoenix's struct rusage lacks ru_maxrss/ru_minflt/ru_majflt and it has no
CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, so source/util/timer.{h,cpp} would not compile.
Timers are an optional profiling aid, unused by STK.

--- a/lib/shaderc/third_party/spirv-tools/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lib/shaderc/third_party/spirv-tools/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -39,6 +39,13 @@
 if("${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}" STREQUAL "Linux")
   add_definitions(-DSPIRV_LINUX)
   set(SPIRV_TIMER_ENABLED ${SPIRV_ALLOW_TIMERS})
+elseif("${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}" STREQUAL "Generic")
+  # STK/Phoenix cross build sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Generic. Treat it as Linux for
+  # SPIRV_LINUX (ANSI colour codes in source/print.cpp only). Do NOT enable
+  # SPIRV_TIMER_ENABLED: Phoenix's struct rusage lacks ru_maxrss/ru_minflt/
+  # ru_majflt and it has no CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, so source/util/timer.* does
+  # not compile. Timers are an optional profiling aid, unused by STK.
+  add_definitions(-DSPIRV_LINUX)
 elseif("${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}" STREQUAL "NintendoSwitch")
     # STK addition treat it as linux, SPIRV_LINUX is used in source/print.cpp:17 only
     add_definitions(-DSPIRV_LINUX)
